---
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";
import { Card, CardGrid } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";
import illustration from "../assets/upskill-illustration.png";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: "UpSkill Design System",
    template: "splash",
    hero: {
      tagline:
        "A design system where AI runs as infrastructure, not as a feature. Machine-readable component contracts tell agents what exists and how it composes, so Claude is called in only where judgment is needed, without 24/7 orchestration.",
      image: { file: illustration, alt: "A designer at a desk surrounded by tool palettes, swatches, and a drawing tablet" },
      actions: [
        { text: "Start here", link: `${base}/start-here/`, icon: "right-arrow" },
        { text: "Agentic moments", link: `${base}/06-agentic-moments/`, variant: "minimal" },
      ],
    },
  }}
>
  <p>
    Most agentic setups keep a model running around the clock, re-reading live APIs on every step. UpSkill does
    the opposite. Every component ships a JSON metadata contract covering its role, props, composition rules and
    accessibility, which gives agents a semantic layer to read instead of guessing. Scripts and CI handle everything repetitive. Claude is invoked only to interpret design intent,
    and it reads small frozen snapshots instead of calling Figma or Airtable directly. The result is team-scale
    rigor that one person can maintain.
  </p>

  <CardGrid>
    <Card title="Three key loops" icon="random">
      <ul>
        <li><a href={`${base}/06-agentic-moments/#the-verified-add-component-loop-concretely`}><strong>Build</strong></a>: Figma to a gated, reviewed React PR.</li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/11-self-improving-loops/#learning-loops`}><strong>Learn</strong></a>: every review finding becomes a rule.</li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/06-agentic-moments/#the-nine-moments`}><strong>Sync</strong></a>: CI flags stale docs; only those sections get rewritten.</li>
      </ul>
    </Card>
    <Card title="User touch points" icon="open-book">
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Airtable</strong>: live inventory of every token and component.</li>
        <li><strong>CLI</strong>: system status at hand for developers.</li>
        <li><strong>Storybook</strong>: the engineer's component reference.</li>
        <li><strong>Docs site</strong>: architecture and decisions, kept current by CI.</li>
      </ul>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>

  <h2>The numbers</h2>
  <CardGrid>
    <Card title="95% fewer API calls" icon="download">One snapshot read replaces 20 live lookups.</Card>
    <Card title="Up to 1M tokens a week saved" icon="clock">On-demand commands replace always-on agents.</Card>
    <Card title="9 of 40 workflows use Claude" icon="setting">The rest are scripts and GitHub Actions.</Card>
    <Card title="58% of bugs caught" icon="approve-check">By a reviewer with no memory of how the component was built.</Card>
  </CardGrid>

  <p>
    Open source on <a href="https://github.com/F4cu/upskill-design-system">GitHub</a>, including the ledger that
    measures whether each agent earns its cost.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>
